it's great to welcome back to the  program today johav dror who is the ceo  and co-founder of pumapay pumapay.io  for more information uh yoav it's great  to have you on today  hi david nice being back here so i mean  let's just first remind the audience  uh tell us a little bit about the  pumapay project  and about your background uh what what  was the idea here  yeah so uh i'm coming from a background  of a  high-risk high transaction uh business  online businesses  and back in the old days in 2017  when the first crypto revolution was  just coming about we started to think  how we can utilize this technology  in our business and after  lots of thinking we came up with a the  conclusion  that what is a massively broken in  any high-risk business is payments so  we decided to fund  a puma pay which is all about crypto  payments  but with a little a twist  uh before puma pay the only type of  transaction you could do is just  a simple push you could send a  crypto to someone else to another party  with poompe  you can deploy advanced billing model  logic onto the blockchain which in  simple words  meaning that you can do subscriptions  and top-ups and  and other billing logics that are very  common in a  high risk especially in iris industries  and  were not available in the blockchain  before so in a nutshell  pumapay is about advanceability models  about subscriptions about top-ups  etc yeah one of the early you know we  for processing subscriptions on our  website we have two integrations we have  a paypal integra  integration and we have a stripe  integration and two of the great things  about that  is we can set up those subscriptions we  can set up  monthly or every number of days or  yearly  and we're essentially pulling those  payments which of course are  pre-authorized and that's a big part of  this being able to have that entire  recurring payment ecosystem people would  come to me and say  you should accept crypto for  subscriptions and i  would say i'm glad to accept it but the  right now someone has to every month  remember to send me a payment there's no  subscription integration  that's what you're tackling for  high-risk industries  correct and not only for high-risk  industries we're tackling it for  any industry we're tackling uh  subscriptions  recurring transactions for crypto in  general  and we have several layers to our  solution first of all  there's the protocol layer where we  enable  all these authorizations and pooling and  reverse  a transaction mechanism via  an architecture of smart contracts that  facilitates this  but on top of that we also added a layer  of products to manage your subscription  as  a as a merchant you want to manage your  subscriptions you want to create  building model widgets to put on your  website so you can collect subscriptions  you want to see your subscribers you  want to be able to  change subscriptions to response to the  request and as a user  you want to be in control of your  subscription you want to be able  to cancel subscription to ask for a  refund etc so we built  a whole layer of products on top of the  protocol to facilitate  this okay so i i want to talk about  some of the key changes for puma pay  version 3.  i think maybe to get into that it would  be good to explain  across crypto over the last several  years  there have been real issues with  transaction fees and  it's not just sometimes the speed with  which  transactions are taking place which on  some networks has slowed down  a lot uh but also the cost of a lot of  these transactions so talk to us a  little bit about that  and then what led you to develop version  three now  yeah so we implemented our first  version of subscriptions i think it was  october or november 2018.  thereafter we continued we added we  built some more products  and we introduced a more a  robust and final a  product toward the end  around let's say september or october  2019  shortly after a we saw the gas prices  started increasing okay our  our implementation is so far on the  ethereum network  and you know ethereum was the gold  standard for a decentralized application  development  and slowly slowly we started seeing the  problems and we we started  getting the feedback from merchants who  integrated with us  and they said hey the the gas prices are  increasing and  it reached a a state where  merchants were had to pay  more than ten dollars to charge a  customer  less than ten dollars so it didn't make  any sense at all  right so and and we just see you know  it's just uh the problem just  uh uh escalates every every week every  month it becomes a a  bigger problem so we went back to the  drawing board and we  tried to find a solution for this  and we evaluated many solutions many  different solutions and  eventually we decided to migrate our  protocol from ethereum  to binance marching and on binance  marching according to  our preliminary calculations we can see  transactions that are a hundred times  faster and 50 times cheaper than what we  currently have  so instead of paying dollars for the gas  phase it's not even something that puma  pay earns  it's just for the blockchain for the  processing the transaction so instead of  paying dollars  merchants will have to pay just cents  that's  uh um i mean that it seems like that  alone could be the difference maker in  terms of adoption right because this is  such a barrier  for many people when they look and they  say okay even if i want to make a  hundred dollar payment and it costs ten  dollars it's just too much  yeah i totally agree but this is not the  only improvement that we're doing i mean  i totally agree that  this was a huge barrier for adoption  another barrier that we discovered uh  at the beginning our approach we said  that we will try to convert  credit card paying users to to become  crypto paying  users and on our first implementation  everyone had to have  a balance in pma tokens so they can  subscribe  and 