nce smart chain  they can transfer it back if they wish  but they can keep it on ethereum nothing  will change we keep our token listed on  the exchanges where we are currently  listed which is  mainly a bittrex okay x uh hitbtc  and several others uh so there is no  need to transfer any tokens anyone can  transfer the tokens through the bridge  but they don't have to they can keep it  there  on the ethereum network and and we we  will continue you know to  support this token as well got it um you  have you know one of the things that's  very common with a lot of blockchain  projects is that  the word decentralized is used  but oftentimes there is not actually  decentralization at least in many  aspects of the project or of how a  certain blockchain works  talk to us a little bit about that i  mean the the pl if i understand  correctly the plan for puma pay  is real decentralization correct  correct you know i'm old enough to  remember  that uh 21 years ago in the  in the dot-com bubble every company  would add  dot-com to their name and their stock  would go berserk so  maybe it has the same effect you know  adding the word decentralized or  decentralization  but in essence a  you know decentralization or  decentralized platform is a platform  that is not governed by any  a single entity and this is what we plan  for the pumapay protocol in the long run  so we have decided as part of this week  we will also introduce another  um participant in our ecosystem  we call it the executor nodes  and in a nutshell it will be  a decentralized version of our existing  back end  so we take our back end the the modules  that are responsible  you know to record the transaction and  remember who do we need to charge and  when  right transferring tokens from this user  to that merchant on this date and that  day  so we just decentralize all this as as a  module as an sdk  that anyone can run on their computer  like they run you know  a mining modules and a  this decentralized network of executor  nodes will be responsible  to post the transactions on behalf of  the merchants and the users  and they will be able also to charge a  small fee  from the merchants for processing their  transactions  saying this any merchant will be able  to be an executor as well and process  their own transactions such that not  only  they won't have any processing fees but  they will also be able to make money by  processing  other merchants uh transactions  merchants that  doesn't want to run a node understood  um last thing what's up ahead on the  roadmap we  you talked a little bit about v3 what  other pumapay projects are on the  horizon now  so v3 is the main thing as part of  v3 there are many things that we're  planning we spoke about  the liquidity pools we spoke about about  the bridge which is already live  we spoke about the executor nodes we're  also  uh we intend to uh  improve the onboarding process for  merchants to our business console we  intend to  ease it up as much as a  regulation permits okay if it's up to me  i wouldn't ask any  kyc from anyone but you know regulation  is a regulation so we'll have to comply  but i want to ease it up both for  merchants and for users  we intend to introduce a web wallet  up until now users have to download our  mobile wallet app which is part of the  system  but at v3 they will be able to use a  meta mask or a a binance wallet or trust  wallet  to do their transactions they'll be able  to connect to a web wallet and manage  all their subscriptions from there  in addition to that we are something  that we spoke about in the past  but we never had a chance to execute but  we  plan to do it after we introduce these  three is uh  introducing plugins for uh you know a  for popular ecommerce uh platforms like  shopify like a wordpress etc  and and in essence our aim is to make  a poompa more accessible both for  merchants and for users  and cheaper and easier and faster and  better  all right we've been speaking with johav  dror who's the ceo  and co-founder of pumapay you can learn  more at pumapay.io  you have always great speaking to you  thank you  same

